{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects","id":1505436,"title":"M20 Effect Duration and Multiple Effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-15T08:52:00-07:00","id":1505436,"title":"M20 Effect Duration and Multiple Effects","content":"I thought that I understood how duration works - overall successes per the duration chart determine how long an Effect is active, or, if using divided successes, addition successes above the base can be spent on duration. When the duration ends, so does the Effect.<br /> <br /> I stumbled across a line that's making me question this though. On p. 528-529 of M20, there is a section How Many Effects Can I Use at Once on the penalties for running multiple effects at once. That's mostly pretty clear, though exactly what constitutes an effect that requires active concentration could be ambiguous.<br /> <br /> What I'm caught up on is the last paragraph, which states that an Effect &quot;that has been cast but whose duration has not yet expired, does not count towards the total.&quot; Their example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Lee Ann enchants a guy, and if - thanks to the number of successes rolled - that enchantment lasts for a week after they part company, then Lee Ann does not have to concentrate on the Effect to keep it going. If she wishes to <i>extend</i> the Effect beyond its original duration, however, then it counts against the number of Effects that character can employ at the same time. </div> </div> </div>This seems to indicate that all spells last indefinitely so long as the mage concentrates on them an accepts a +1 difficulty to casting for every 2 spells active beyond the initial duration. I can't find anything else in the book about this, though, so I'm not sure if there's any other context that would change that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6927-gillestrilleuze","name":"GillesTrilleuze","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T12:51:54-07:00","id":1505495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GillesTrilleuze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects#post1505436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to indicate that all spells last indefinitely so long as the mage concentrates on them an accepts a +1 difficulty to casting for every 2 spells active beyond the initial duration. I can't find anything else in the book about this, though, so I'm not sure if there's any other context that would change that interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no other context anywhere, but yes - essentially, a spell you do not usually need to concentrate one, turns into one needing active concentration to keep up as soon as you keep it beyond the rolled duration.<br /> <br /> Which I really like, but the question then is - do spells you have to concentrate on in the first place essentially have umlinited duration (as long as you concentrate)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T20:44:22-07:00","id":1505632,"title":"","content":"My gut instinct is if you don't invest in Duration, an Effect can only be effectively concentrated on until the end of the scene. Unless you have some other Effect (probably Mind + possibly Prime) that lets you concentrate longer.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not inclined to commit to that answer, as I'm not convinced it's worth being so restrictive.<br /> <br /> I <i>definitely</i> think you can't concentrate on a spell if you're asleep (again, except with a Mind Effect to keep a splinter of consciousness running). So the normal upper limit for a Mage's concentration is gated by how well they roll Stamina to stay awake (AND focused; a Mage caught in sleep-deprived delirium isn't concentrating on shit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T13:33:17-07:00","id":1506525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1505632#post1505632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My gut instinct is if you don't invest in Duration, an Effect can only be effectively concentrated on until the end of the scene. Unless you have some other Effect (probably Mind + possibly Prime) that lets you concentrate longer.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not inclined to commit to that answer, as I'm not convinced it's worth being so restrictive.<br /> <br /> I <i>definitely</i> think you can't concentrate on a spell if you're asleep (again, except with a Mind Effect to keep a splinter of consciousness running).</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me like a cool, nice, good, and interesting option and capability for a Mage (including for a Nephandus or a Technocrat, or a Solificati Alchemist, or a Verbenae Witch) to be able to actively cast and channel Magick Effects while asleep or resting.<br /> <br /> This definitely feels like it is in like with how Mage:the Ascension has been written, illustrated, designed, and developed since the first books and supplements of the 1st edition of this good, interesting, intricate, and wonderous role-playing game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:12:13-07:00","id":1512952,"title":"","content":"And what if the effect is a physical mutation? A mage with the life sphere could use it to increase it's strength, and if the success allow him to keep the effect for 1 week it does not require active concentration. But can the mage use the life sphere again and give himself another mutation, will he get an higher difficulty to accumulate those 2 effect or can he accumulate freely long-lasting effect of this type?<br /> <br /> Because knowing that whith enough success a mage can make a permanent effect it could be hard to manage for the ST i think, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T15:15:59-07:00","id":1513008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1512952#post1512952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what if the effect is a physical mutation? A mage with the life sphere could use it to increase it's strength, and if the success allow him to keep the effect for 1 week it does not require active concentration. But can the mage use the life sphere again and give himself another mutation, will he get an higher difficulty to accumulate those 2 effect or can he accumulate freely long-lasting effect of this type?<br /> <br /> Because knowing that whith enough success a mage can make a permanent effect it could be hard to manage for the ST i think, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the effect is on duration (and locked if needed), then it doesn't count for concentrating effect penalty. So, yes, mages can have several effects with duration running without any penalty. That's more or less how they are able to survive in WoD<br /> <br /> About permanent effects, you need to spend xp or deal with permadox (if it's vulgar) and/or pattern bleeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T10:05:18-07:00","id":1513087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513008#post1513008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About permanent effects, you need to spend xp or deal with permadox (if it's vulgar) and/or pattern bleeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using special or magic objects and items ( artifacts, talismans, and other types ) could also help in regard to this. Extensively working in one place or location is another possibility. <br /> <br /> Also - I think that each group and faction of Mages does have Spells, Rotes, and Effects in which they specialize. Among these there could be some enduring / permament Effects which would be easier to learn, and to cast, and to maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T12:57:23-07:00","id":1513104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513087#post1513087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using special or magic objects and items ( artifacts, talismans, and other types ) could also help in regard to this. Extensively working in one place or location is another possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Trinkets are even better for this, since they do not require Prime and have no requisite of sphere level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513087#post1513087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also - I think that each group and faction of Mages does have Spells, Rotes, and Effects in which they specialize. Among these there could be some enduring / permament Effects which would be easier to learn, and to cast, and to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rule wise, the only thing that changes is your affinity sphere and personalized instruments. Nothing more than that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T16:18:47-07:00","id":1513131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513008#post1513008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About permanent effects, you need to spend xp or deal with permadox (if it's vulgar) and/or pattern bleeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to get to strength 6 or more with the life sphere and get enough success to make the duration permanent as decribed on the table p.504 you still need xp?<br /> As i'm quite a newbie on mage there's some things i still don't get, a mage wanting to accomplish any kind of effet can use a ritual and/or accumulate success turn after turn to accomplish them? Seems pretty difficult for the st...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T17:57:51-07:00","id":1513140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513131#post1513131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to get to strength 6 or more with the life sphere and get enough success to make the duration permanent as decribed on the table p.504 you still need xp?<br /> As i'm quite a newbie on mage there's some things i still don't get, a mage wanting to accomplish any kind of effet can use a ritual and/or accumulate success turn after turn to accomplish them? Seems pretty difficult for the st...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, getting 6 in an attribute would give you permadox (and iirc, pattern bleeding too) until you pay for it with xp (at half price) or somehow undo the change.<br /> <br /> There are two ways to make extended rolls: rituals or &quot;picking where you left off&quot;. Rituals can be dangerous, sometimes exhausting and have a roll limit (WP+Arete rolls). The &quot;picking&quot; thing let's you keep rolling at +1 diff, which means you can't keep on forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T01:30:49-07:00","id":1513176,"title":"","content":"The picking thing, if the pc is trying to make a spell that need 8 success, he will get the +1 diff immediatly on his second, third, fourth roll (cumulatingly), or just if he stop and picking where he left some turn after?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T12:32:25-07:00","id":1513221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513176#post1513176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The picking thing, if the pc is trying to make a spell that need 8 success, he will get the +1 diff immediatly on his second, third, fourth roll (cumulatingly), or just if he stop and picking where he left some turn after?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he needs 8 successes but only got 3, for example, independently of the Arete rank, he has made a partial success and the spell wont work exactly as intended. The mage can keep rolling at +1 diff until 8 successes are achieved. Each Arete roll beaides the first one (original), add +1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T13:45:48-07:00","id":1513229,"title":"","content":"Diff +1 on the second roll, +2 on the third and so on until he achieve his spell, and i suppose it can go beyond the usual limit of +3/-3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T04:36:03-07:00","id":1513280,"title":"","content":"Yes, for Picking Up rules you add +1 difficulty on each subsequent roll. If it were an intended ritual, you would only add +1 difficulty after each roll with no successes. <br /> <br /> I don't see why this would be an exception to the +3 cap. In most cases, a spell that reaches that cap is outside of the Mage's reasonable abilities anyways and should be done as a ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:23:46-07:00","id":1513324,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26839_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26839\" data-vbnamecard=\"26839\">Cain Loup-Noir</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> I couldn't find a quote that says that this rule is above the +3 cap, so I think it still have this limit. This would mean that after the 4 roll (3 beyond the original) difficulty does not change.<br /> <br /> However, if you are using means to decrease difficulty, this means that you can get more than +3, although not in total.<br /> <br /> So, if your diff is 7 and you manage to get -3 by any means you will keep rolling at diff 5 for the second roll, 6 for the third, until 10 is reached (+3 cap). If the cap stops beyond 10, you can use threshold rule.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:29:07-07:00","id":1513326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1505436-m20-effect-duration-and-multiple-effects?p=1513104#post1513104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. Trinkets are even better for this, since they do not require Prime and have no requisite of sphere level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talens - or other special and magical objects - traded with or 